WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
G’day. Jonesy here, introducing you to

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.270
Geoff’s Guide. Let’s work through the tabs,

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.590
from left to right. Form gives you

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.430
our original view of the race: the

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.510
shortlist, the full field, and the form

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.830
behind each runner. Start here to see

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.830
who comes out on top. Late mail

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.430
brings in what changes as the day

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.550
unfolds: conditions, scratchings, riders and

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.110
fresh information. See our revised selection

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.030
beside the original, and understand what

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.670
moved it. Tips brings together leading racing

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.150
tipsters. Explore the collective view, then

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.017
open each tip to see the reasoning,

00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:33.910
the assumed conditions, and the run that

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.870
horse needs. The Ladder connects the form.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.550
If two horses have met, who beat

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.470
whom, and by how much? If they

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.470
haven’t, a shared opponent can help connect

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.070
them. It’s another way to weigh the

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.150
evidence, rather than a guaranteed finishing

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.310
order. And Results shows how Geoff’s

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.670
selections performed, alongside the jockeys,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.003
trainers and tipsters having a day out.

00:00:52.987 --> 00:00:54.550
Come back five minutes before the jump

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.230
for the latest saved late mail and

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.089
race preview—Geoff’s edge. Happy punting!
